   "source": [
    "For $f(x) = x_1^2 + 100x_2^2$:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Gradient ($\\nabla f$): $\\begin{bmatrix} 2x_1 \\\\ 200x_2 \\end{bmatrix}$\n",
    "\n",
    "- Hessian ($H$): $\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 200 \\end{bmatrix}$\n",
    "\n",
    "The Condition Number here is $200 / 2 = 100$. Generally, the higher the condition number, the harder it is for Gradient Descent to converge."
   ]
  },
